From f762317982cfcae5cf343402161f3d50660caa32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: samusun343-ai <samusun343-ai@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:27:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] ASoC: add ROHM BU26154 codec and MXS machine support

The SHARP Brain boards carry a ROHM BU26154MUV codec, but the
Brainux device tree names the i.MX28 EVK sgtl5000 (I2C 0x0a),
which is not populated: probing fails with -ENXIO and no ALSA
card is ever created.

Add, from the public BU26154 datasheet (Rev.002):
- a codec driver (sound/soc/codecs/bu26154.c) implementing the
  part's INDEX register protocol on I2C 0x1a, its clock divider
  selection for a 256/512/1024 x fs MCLKI, playback/capture DAI
  and the PDATT/RDVOL/AVVOL volume and mute controls;
- a machine driver (sound/soc/mxs/mxs-bu26154.c) in the
  mxs-sgtl5000 pattern: SAIF0 playback / SAIF1 capture, SAIF
  MCLK at 512 x fs feeding the codec, mxs_saif_get_mclk()
  claimed in probe;
- DT glue replacing the sgtl5000 node with the BU26154 and
  Kconfig/defconfig wiring (built-in: the distribution rootfs
  ships no /lib/modules or Module.symvers, so out-of-tree
  modules cannot be used with the stock kernel).
